OL,3,GNEWSAChildren in Need funds
OL,4,Alife-changing, charity says
OL,5,
OL,6,FFunding from BBC Children in Need is
OL,7,Fbeing described as life-changing by one
OL,8,FGuernsey charity.
OL,10,FAutism Guernsey was recently given
OL,11,F#84,000 pounds to spend over three
OL,12,Fyears, helping children with a new
OL,13,Fmental health and wellbeing project.
OL,15,FJulia Watts, the charity's CEO, said
OL,16,Feveryone involved was so thankful for
OL,17,Fthe support that would allow them to
OL,18,Fwork with 100 children: "I mean we are
OL,19,Fso grateful, I don't know how to
OL,20,Fexpress that in words.
OL,23,APub: 13-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
